# release-notes loads optional .env locally. Never commit real credentials.
OPENAI_API_KEY=
# Optional override; otherwise communique.toml selects gpt-5.4-nano.
# COMMUNIQUE_MODEL=gpt-5.4-nano
# Generation sends git history, selected diffs/source, and configuration context
# to OpenAI and incurs API charges, even with --dry-run. No fixed total cost cap.
# No GITHUB_TOKEN or FORGEJO_TOKEN is needed for generation. GitHub reads are disabled.
# Start before tagging: mise run release-notes -- HEAD --label v1.0.0
# --label names files only; review/edit the release title as well as the body.
# Without tags, Communique uses root..HEAD (the root commit itself is excluded).
# Tracked working-tree files may be read as context; commit intended changes first.
# Review .robin/releases/v1.0.0.{md,draft.json,review.md,migration.md} manually.
# Copy ONLY approved Markdown to .forgejo/workflows/release-notes/v1.0.0.md,
# commit it, then tag that commit. Generation never stages, commits, or publishes.
# Review artifacts share the release staging directory: remove/move these extras
# before release-publish, whose validator requires an exact artifact set.
